{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>This is the Torah.</b> One who comes to rule on negaim must know how to distinguish between two types, even though they are one in species, as it says (Deuteronomy 17:8): בֵּין נֶגַע לָנֶגַע." "<b>For every plague of tzara'at and for the netek.</b> For even though both are tzara'at of human skin, nevertheless they differ in this: the netek is judged not by appearances alone, but its ruling is like the turning of hair white or black hair, whereas all other types of tzara'at are judged by appearances alone."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:36.315698692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}